<font size="3"><b>Skiing in Amherst also (Meg)</b></font><br>
<i>Posted 3/7 by steve</i><p><p>
<p>
Here I am in Amherst, the first Sunday morning in a long, long time to be here and to be by myself.  Kind of wierd. Lijke Dedie and Peter,  I went skiing this morning, up across the golf course and into the woods, along the Robert Frost trail and almost to Leverett, around and back.  Because the snow fell onto softening and wet ground, I ran into what yesterday morning must have been a vernal pool, an early sign of Spring, now covered with 6 inches of snow and blowing wind.  But it was still wet underneath and made a mess on the bottom of my skis. I don't understand how snow could pile up on a pool of water.  The snow must be insulation to keep the water from freezing, but what holds it up?   I wonder if any peepers were suckered into birth by the warm days of last week.  The ground has warmed up enough now, maybe they would make it.  I reversed my usual circular route to have the whipping north wind at my back instead of in my face.  Tonight will be a real deep freeze.<br>
<br>
Matt flew to Rome on Friday night  with his girl friend Emily, her father, her sister and her best friend.  They made it to the youth hostel but Matt's pack never made it off the plane and his phone card doesn't work.  He managed to get an email message through and sounds cheerful.  He will travel with this crew for two weeks and then he will be more or less on his own for 6 weeks.  Steve and my bro Jon in Paris are the fallbacks if disaster strikes, but he should be OK.  He just turned 17 last week, a little young for a solo European adventure, but he really needed to get out of Amherst, so ...<br>
<br>
Simon is spending the weekend with his peeps; right now a gang of them are  sledding on the golf course, temporarily 10-yeas-old again.  Makes me happy.<br>
<br>
I am going to England on Thursday to celegrate March 14 with the birthday boy. I can't wait. The understantement of the year.   Any messages or items anyone would like me to take, let me know by Wednesday.  I will probably bring Sandy out to the farm for a week-end sleep-over with her friend Jazzie and could pick messages up for Steve.  Carl and Peg: where is the best place to leave a car in Boston?  Aylewife?  Your street?  Login long-term parking?? My flight is Thursday morning at 8:45.  Do you have a spare bed on Wednesday night if I come in then?  I can't decide  whether to come in Wednesday night or do it all on Thursday.<br>
<br>
How do you all decide whether a message should be public or private?  Guess I'll be public with this one!<br>
<br>
I will type (Meg) after my titles so you know it isn't really Steve.  Steve has to pay a hefty fee for time on the Internet so he might not be posting very many messages on the farm page.  He said he will check the page regularly.  This home page is such a terrific idea.  Thanks Simon!!<br>
<br>
Meg<p>
